he anchors '(2026-05-01)' and 'evidence-store sibling'; pattern THEN: require every substantive claim to point to evidence.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Anchor the completion claim: name the concrete artifact (evidence-store sibling), the step (INSTANTIATE), and a date, so a reader can check it rather than trust it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Source fragment 19-79: 'INSTANTIATE complete (2026-05-01) for evidence-store sibling'; pattern IF: outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission's status line makes a substantive completion claim that other agents and the operator must be able to verify."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: 'Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation'; the fragment itself is an unadorned status assertion unless anchored.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "A bare 'done' assertion would be indistinguishable from confabulation; the claim is only meaningful if it points at checkable evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'Evidence transforms agent output from trust me to check this'; the dated, named fragment is what makes the status line checkable.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The claim moves the mission record from 'trust me' to 'check this', enabling later verification and correction of the INSTANTIATE step's status."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [0], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion"} {:pattern-rationale "Bypassing the queue cadence is a deliberate escalation whose cost is weighed against the risk of waiting, exactly the trade this pattern names.", :fragment-span {:start 84, :end 135}, :occurrence-id ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1], :roles ["contrast" "context"], :source-sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab", :sentence-id "s1", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk", :objects {:G {:text "    This preserves speed on low-stakes actions while protecting high-stakes decisions.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'STOP-THE-LINE HOT-FIX, outside normal queue cadence'; pattern THEN: escalate when risk cost exceeds a threshold and log the comparison basis.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Escalate out of cadence explicitly and visibly: stop the line, label the action a hot-fix so the exception is on the record."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 84-105 'STOP-THE-LINE HOT-FIX' declares the intervention; pattern IF: a decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A defect in an evidence-store sibling may carry material risk to the boot-reachable chain, warranting an interruptive decision."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination costs discourage escalation, while risk-blind escalation wastes time on low-stakes work.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 107-135 'outside normal queue cadence'; pattern HOWEVER: coordination costs discourage escalation while risk-blind escalation wastes time.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Normal queue cadence would defer the fix (coordination discipline), but waiting risks letting a high-stakes defect ride the queue."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Estimate risk cost (impact x likelihood) and compare it to coordination cost. Escalate when risk cost exceeds a defined threshold, and log the comparison basis.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: preserves speed on low-stakes actions while protecting high-stakes decisions; the fragment names both the stop and the cadence exception.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Marking the exception preserves queue speed for ordinary work while protecting the high-stakes fix from cadence delay."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [1], :pattern "agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk"} {:pattern-rationale "Work moves to Codex through a durable GitHub issue so the receiving agent keeps the context, the pattern's core move.", :fragment-span {:start 139, :end 200}, :occurrence-id ["agent/handoff-preserves-context" 2], :roles ["action" "dependency"], :source-sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3", :sentence-id "s1", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/handoff-preserves-context", :objects {:G {:text "    Handoffs convert ephemeral session state into persistent project state. They enable distributed and asynchronous work without context collapse.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab exports session context to `lab/raw`, `lab/stubs`, and `lab/trace` (`dev/lab-export-claude.clj`), plus summaries via `fulab-summary` and `fulab-session-report`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'via GitHub issue #65'; pattern THEN: define a handoff record capturing state, decisions, open questions, next actions.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Transfer the remaining work through a durable, tracked handoff record — GitHub issue #65 — rather than an untracked mention."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Continuity matters: the work is incremental, context is expensive to rebuild, or progress would be lost.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Fragment 139-200: 'Three remaining siblings handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65'; pattern IF: continuity matters, context is expensive to rebuild.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The three remaining siblings are incremental work whose context (what INSTANTIATE already established) is expensive to rebuild."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Without explicit handoff, successors face cold starts: they repeat discoveries, miss constraints, or contradict prior decisions.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: without explicit handoff, successors face cold starts; the fragment records the transfer to a new agent.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Handing work to a different agent risks a cold start: Codex could repeat discoveries or miss the decisions already made for the completed sibling."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Define a handoff record that captures: current state hypothesis, decisions made and why, open questions, scope boundaries, next actions, evidence/trail anchors, and any provisional-claim ledger. Emit it at session end or when transferring to another agent.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: handoffs convert ephemeral session state into persistent project state; the tracked issue number in the fragment is the persistent anchor.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The issue converts ephemeral session state into persistent project state so the sibling work continues asynchronously without context collapse."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "agent/handoff-preserves-context"}], :edges [{:from ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 0], :to ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1], :kind :contrasts-with, :from-fragment 0, :to-fragment 1, :from-roles ["action" "goal"], :to-roles ["contrast" "context"]} {:from ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1], :to ["agent/handoff-preserves-context" 2], :kind :context-enables, :from-fragment 1, :to-fragment 2, :from-roles ["contrast" "context"], :to-roles ["action" "dependency"]}], :precedence [["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 0] ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1] ["agent/handoff-preserves-context" 2]]}}, :reading-pin {:analysis-digest "b8206e8c53d3117727